This port contains no C code from any of the above. Its behaviour was written
from descriptions of the upstream program (docs/research/) and is verified by
replaying the upstream recordings.


Graphics and sound data
-----------------------

The graphics (sprites, character set, title screen, palettes) and the sound
and music tables used by this program are derived from Digger Remastered.
They are read as data from the Digger Remastered sources as distributed in
sobomax/digger, and are covered by the same GNU General Public License grant
made by Andrew Jenner. The VGA graphics were redrawn by Andrew Jenner; the
sound tables and CGA graphics originate in the 1983 game and are distributed
under the permission of Rob Sleath as relayed by Andrew Jenner.

The music comprises third-party compositions: "Popcorn" (composed by Gershon
Kingsley), the William Tell Overture (Gioachino Rossini) and the Funeral March
from Piano Sonata No. 2 (Frederic Chopin).

The basis for these statements is recorded in docs/research/07-web-research.md
(section A.5, "Licence and copyright"). This notice is not legal advice.
